<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 9.029 percent on Monday from 8.950 percent at the previous auction on May 19.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1,312.3 million pounds, replace bills worth 926.975 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 1.1 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):.</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 25, 1997 (Nov 18, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.029 percent (8.950).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,312.3 million (991.725 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,432.300 million (2,419.025 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.000-9.496 percent (8.751-8.985).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.000-10.200 percent (8.751-10.200).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 125 (90).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 127 (236).</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds.</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
